WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.213
Unit 1: reading the workbook.

2
00:00:02.213 --> 00:00:06.356
Telemetry completeness comes
first, because every other tab

3
00:00:06.356 --> 00:00:10.337
depends on its sources: a dark
source is a high-severity task.

4
00:00:10.337 --> 00:00:14.659
Then each tab in turn, and each
row that needs work becomes,

5
00:00:14.659 --> 00:00:17.325
or is matched to, a task with an owner.

6
00:00:17.325 --> 00:00:21.225
Entra Health and the I T S M
queue are worked where they live.

7
00:00:21.225 --> 00:00:26.212
The workbook never closes a task, pages
anyone, or proves a check happened.

8
00:00:26.212 --> 00:00:31.262
And the rule: an empty queue over a
stale source reads stale, never clear.

9
00:00:31.262 --> 00:00:35.374
A missed probe shows yesterday's
verdict, so its tab is stale too.

10
00:00:35.374 --> 00:00:39.867
A synchronization server or domain
controller that stops sending

11
00:00:39.867 --> 00:00:43.637
isn't an empty list: it's a row
with an old heartbeat, flagged.

12
00:00:43.637 --> 00:00:49.530
And the replication probe needs Enterprise
Admins or equivalent to read replication,

13
00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:52.370
so it runs only on a Tier
0 host, or not at all.
